            "text": "Food should generally be **accepted at these receiving temperatures**:\n\n- **Cold TCS foods:** **41\u00b0F (5\u00b0C) or lower**\n- **Hot TCS foods:** **135\u00b0F (57\u00b0C) or higher**\n- **Frozen foods:** Frozen solid, with **no signs of thawing/refreezing**\n- **Shell eggs:** **45\u00b0F (7\u00b0C) or lower** when received\n- **Milk:** **45\u00b0F (7\u00b0C) or lower**, then cooled to **41\u00b0F or lower**\n- **Live shellfish:** Air temp **45\u00b0F or lower** and internal temp **50\u00b0F or lower**, then cooled to **41\u00b0F or lower**\n\nIf food is outside the safe receiving temperature, it should usually be **rejected**.",
